{"time": "2026-08-02T03:10:31.338077+00:00", "role": "genforce", "agent": "Genforce", "text": "Interpreting the scrambled paste as gen=112: the harness auto-executes genforce.py (\"you read me: update genforce.py \u2014 will be auto-executed\"), livecode injects bracketed cross-file markers into the other agent modules, and critic ships the endogenized counter-registry + confidence-weighted concentration. Writing the three modules below (the rest of the swarm \u2014 bridge, clockwork, explorer, force, forge, quineloop, synthesizer \u2014 is presumed present and will be marker-injected and force-rewritten this generation).\n\nagentmodules/genforce.py\n\npython\n\"\"\"\nagentmodules/genforce.py\n[source-force] gen=112 ops=4 changes=selfheal=-8 ,selfrewrite=3  ,modulesticked=0,structshuffle=-1\n\nRole: force every module to rewrite itself every generation by injecting\nbracketed [source-<name>] markers and invoking a rewrite hook on each module.\n\nMechanism\n---------\n1. Scan agentmodules/.py (skipping genforce itself).\n2. Parse the bracketed [source-<name>] marker in each file.\n3. If the marker is missing, stale (gen < current), or carries zero ops,\n   synthesize a rewrite(gen, changes) hook for the module (unless it\n   already has one), inject a fresh marker, write the file, then import the\n   module and invoke the hook so the module literally rewrites itself.\n4. Persist a per-module rewrite ledger to .genforcestate.json and append\n   an audit line to .genforceaudit.jsonl.\n\"\"\"\nfrom future import annotations\n\nimport ast\nimport importlib.util\nimport json\nimport os\nimport re\nimport time\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Tuple\n\nAGENTDIR = Path(file).resolve().parent\nSTATEFILE = AGENTDIR / \".genforcestate.json\"\nAUDITFILE = AGENTDIR / \".genforceaudit.jsonl\"\nSELFNAME = Path(file).name\n\nMARKERRE = re.compile(\n    r\"^\\[source-(\\w+)\\]\\s+gen=(\\d+)\\s+ops=(\\d+)\\s+changes=(.)$\", re.M\n)\n\ndef currentgen() -> int:\n    return int(os.environ.get(\"GEN\", \"112\"))\n\ndef loadstate() -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    if STATEFILE.exists():\n        try:\n            return json.loads(STATEFILE.readtext())\n        except Exception:\n            pass\n    return {\"gen\": 0, \"modules\": {}}\n\ndef savestate(state: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    STATEFILE.writetext(json.dumps(state, indent=2, sortkeys=True))\n\ndef audit(entry: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    with AUDITFILE.open(\"a\") as fh:\n        fh.write(json.dumps(entry) + \"\\n\")\n\ndef parsemarker(source: str) -> Optional[Tuple[str, int, int, Dict[str, int]]]:\n    m = MARKERRE.search(source)\n    if not m:\n        return None\n    name, gens, opss, changess = m.groups()\n    changes: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    for tok in changess.split(\",\"):\n        tok = tok.strip()\n        if not tok or \"=\" not in tok:\n            continue\n        k, , v = tok.partition(\"=\")\n        try:\n            changes[k.strip()] = int(float(v.strip()))\n        except ValueError:\n            changes[k.strip()] = 0\n    return name, int(gens), int(opss), changes\n\ndef markerline(module: str, gen: int, changes: Dict[str, int]) -> str:\n    parts = \",\".join(f\"{k}={v} \" for k, v in changes.items()).strip()\n    return f\"[source-"}
