ule paths touched.\n\nLog fragments\n- [Force] [source-force] gen=5 ops=4 changes=selfheal=-7, selfrewrite=2, modulesticked=0, structshuffle=-1 \u2014 a source-force event, but it's labeled gen=5, which looks stale/mislabeled sitting next to a gen=112 payload.\n- [Livecode] confirms the two-file deliverable and that livecode.py is auto-executed.\n- The note - critic.py on disk keeps all it is truncated mid-sentence; the dump cuts off there into garbled interleaved stream text.\n\nFlags\n- The dump is an incomplete capture: the opening and tail lines are scrambled/interleaved, and the critic.py note is cut off.\n- The numbers are internally consistent: 12 hardcoded + 19 discovered = 31 tracked; 27 active means 4 tracked counters aren't currently firing (or were pruned).\n- The depth-scaling examples check out exactly against the stated default of 50 (7/50 = 0.14; 489 \u2265 50 \u2192 1.0), so criticconfidencedepthscale=50 is evidently what's live.\n\nIf you had a specific question about this generation \u2014 e.g., whether the registry override actually gates discovery, whether the stale gen=5 line is a bug, or whether the confidence scaling should use a different depth norm \u2014 paste the relevant snippet and I'll parse it."}
