FICATION AGAINST THE TOPIC HEADER\n-------------------------------------\n| Topic claim | Reconstruction result |\n|---|---|\n| 12 hardcoded keys gone; 31 tracked (12 + 19 new) | dynamic discovery; tracked count = len(found keys) |\n| 27 active, 614 ops | reported as counterkeysactive / totalops |\n| thin 7-op monopoly \u2192 eff 0.14 | 7/50 = 0.14 \u2713 (smoke-tested) |\n| deep 489-op monopoly \u2192 eff 1.0 | min(1.0, 489/50) = 1.0 \u2713 (smoke-tested) |\n| criticconfidencedepthscale genome-tunable, default 50 | genome.get(\"criticconfidencedepthscale\", 50) \u2713 |\n| registry overrides discovery; evolvable by self-mutator | resolvecounterkeys + persistence \u2713 |\n| rawconcentration / confidence / depthavgops persisted | criticlast + top-level mirrors \u2713 |\n| noveltypressure 0.6335 smoke-verified | kept as genome-tunable default 0.6335 (exact formula was not in the surviving header, so it is preserved as a tunable rather than re-derived) |\n\nDROP-IN INSTRUCTIONS\n--------------------\nSave as agentmodules/critic.py. The driver calls run(genome) (contract\nassumed \u2014 the original payload truncated at \"the driver calls ...\").\nRun python -m agentmodules.critic to execute the smoke test; both\nmonopoly-confidence numbers reproduce the topic header exactly.\n\nIf the driver's real call signature differs from run(genome), or if more of\nthe original source exists on disk, diff this reconstruction against it before\nletting the swarm mutate it \u2014 a self-mutator may be operating on the\nevolvable criticcounterregistry field, and the registry contents are\nauthoritative once present."}
