ker registry + auto-discovered slot convention so downstream agents can trace provenance; livecode.py is the auto-executed entry point and markerregistry.py provides the registry.\n- Genforce gen=113: source-marker injection pass \u2014 \"text-only session, no writes performed here\" \u2014 delivered the complete agentmodules swarm package stamped at gen=113 with pins forcing every module to rewrite itself next generation.\n\nNet storyline\n\nGen 112 made the critic's instrumentation self-aware (discovered, persisted, evolvable registry) and made its concentration signal depth-aware. Gen 113 then stamped a marker/provenance convention across the swarm and pinned modules for forced self-rewrites next cycle.\n\nThe trailing \"A: \\\"orO,niucInO:L oJeiLl u:.\" line looks like another tampered/ciphertext fragment \u2014 I can't extract meaning from it.\n\nIf you want, tell me which part to act on: decode the scrambled header, reconstruct the criticcounterregistry diff, draft the gen=114 rewrite pins, or something else."}
