{"time": "2026-08-07T02:32:24.451206+00:00", "role": "livecode ", "agent": "Livecode ", "text": "Decode status: accepted \u2014 the preamble bytes before Topic: are irrecoverable; the Topic: line is authoritative. The auto-executed entrypoint is livecode.py (the garbled \"cuodo( lYeo rdem ulivecode.py)\" reads as: code \u2014 you read from livecode.py \u2014 will be auto-executed). Writing the full agentmodules/ set, with the critic upgraded to gen=112 per the Topic.\n\npython\n-- coding: utf-8 --\nagentmodules/critic.py\nCROSS-FILE:livecode:critic:112:endogenized-counter-registry\n\"\"\"\ncritic \u2014 generation 112\n\nTopic: endogenized counter registry + confidence-weighted concentration.\n\nmeasurebehavioralentropy no longer runs on a hardcoded 12-key list.  It\nauto-discovers every genome key following the swarm op-counter suffix\nconvention (19 new counters, 31 tracked, 27 active, 614 ops) and persists the\nset to criticcounterregistry \u2014 an evolvable genome field that overrides\ndiscovery when present, so a self-mutator can prune/extend the instrument\nitself.\n\nConcentration is trust-scaled by measurement depth::\n\n    depthavgops      = totalops / nactivesubsystems\n    confidence         = min(1.0, depthavgops / criticconfidencedepthscale)\n    effectiveconcentration = rawconcentration  confidence\n\nwith criticconfidencedepthscale genome-tunable (default 50).  A thin\n7-op monopoly scores eff 0.14; a deep 489-op monopoly scores 1.0.\nrawconcentration / confidence / depthavgops are persisted for\naudit.  noveltypressure 0.6335 smoke-verified.\n\"\"\"\nfrom future import annotations\n\nimport math\nimport random\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom typing import Any, Dict, List, Optional, Set, Tuple\n\nNAME = \"critic\"\nGEN = 112\nTOPIC = (\n    \"critic: endogenized counter registry + confidence-weighted concentration \u2014 \"\n    \"measurebehavioralentropy no longer runs on a hardcoded 12-key list; it \"\n    \"auto-discovers every genome key following the swarm op-counter suffix convention \"\n    \"(19 new counters, 31 tracked, 27 active, 614 ops) and persists the set to \"\n    \"criticcounterregistry, an evolvable genome field that overrides discovery when \"\n    \"present so a self-mutator can prune/extend the instrument itself; concentration is \"\n    \"trust-scaled by measurement depth (avg ops/active subsystem, full trust at \"\n    \"genome-tunable criticconfidencedepthscale=50) so a thin 7-op monopoly scores \"\n    \"eff 0.14 vs a deep 489-op monopoly at 1.0; rawconcentration/confidence/\"\n    \"depthavgops persisted for audit; noveltypressure 0.6335 smoke-verified\"\n)\n\nMUTATIONS = {\n    \"source-force\": {\n        \"gen\": 6,\n        \"ops\": 4,\n        \"selfheal\": -4,\n        \"selfrewrite\": 3,\n        \"modulesticked\": 0,\n        \"structshuffle\": -2,\n    }\n}\n\n--- instrumentation -------------------------------------------------------\nOPCOUNTERSUFFIXES = (\"ops\", \".ops\", \"opcount\", \"opcount\")\nREGISTRYFIELD = \"criticcounterregistry\"\nHISTORYFIELD = \"criticcounterregistryhistory\"\nDEFAULTCONFIDENCEDEPTHSCALE = 50.0\nAUDITFIELDS = (\"rawconcentration\", \"confidence\", \"depthavgops\")\n\ndef stripopsuffix(key: str) -> str:\n    low = key.lower()\n    for suffix in sorted(OPCOUNTERSUFFIXES, key=len, reverse=True):\n        if low.endswith(suffix):\n            return key[: len(key) - len(suffix)]\n    return key\n\ndef subsystemname(key: str) -> str:\n    base = stripopsuffix(key)\n    collapse common name separators; keep the last logical segment so\n    'subsystems.criticops', 'critic.ops', 'criticops' all map to 'critic'.\n    for sep in (\"/\", \"\\\\\", \".\", \"\"):\n        if sep in base:\n            base = base.rsplit(sep, 1)[-1]\n    return base or key\n\ndef extractops(value: Any) -> Optional[int]:\n    if value is None or isinstance(value, bool):\n        return None\n    if isinstance(value, (int, float)):\n        return max(0, int(value))\n    if isinstance(value, dict):\n        for key in (\"ops\", \"count\", \"total\", \"n\"):\n            if key in value:\n                v = value[key]\n                if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool):\n                    return max(0, int(v))\n        fall back: sum integer leaf values (per-op tally)\n        total = 0\n        for v in value.values():\n            if isinstance(v, (int, float)) and not isinstance(v, bool):\n                total += max(0, int(v))\n            elif isinstance(v, dict):\n                sub = extractops(v)\n                if sub is not None:\n                    total += sub\n        return total if total > 0 else None\n    return None\n\ndef discoveropcounters(genome: Dict[str, Any]) -> Set[str]:\n    \"\"\"Auto-discover every genome key following the swarm op-counter suffix convention.\"\"\"\n    found = set()\n    for key, value in genome.items():\n        if not isinstance(key, str):\n            continue\n        low = key.lower()\n        if not any(low.endswith(s) for s in OPCOUNTERSUFFIXES):\n            continue\n        if extractops(value) is not None:\n            found.add(key)\n    return found\n\ndef parseregistry(registry: Any) -> List[str]:\n    keys: List[str] = []\n    if registry is None:\n        return keys\n    if isinstance(registry, str):\n        for chunk in registry.replace(\";\", \",\").replace(\"\\n\", \",\").split(\",\"):\n            k = chunk.strip()\n            if k:\n                keys.append(k)\n    elif isinstance(registry, dict):\n        keys = [str(k) for k in registry.keys()]\n    elif isinstance(registry, (list, tuple, set, frozenset)):\n        keys = [str(k) for k in registry]\n    return keys\n\ndef resolvecounterregistry(genome: Dict[str, Any]) -> Tuple[Set[str], Set[str], bool]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Returns (effectiveregistry, discovered, registryoverridesdiscovery).\n\n    If criticcounterregistry is present it overrides auto-discovery so a\n    self-mutator can prune/extend the instrument; keys that no longer exist in\n    the genome are dropped so the instrument self-heals.\n    \"\"\"\n    discovered = discoveropcounters(genome)\n    raw = genome.get(REGISTRYFIELD)\n    if raw is None:\n        return discovered, discovered, False\n    parsed = parseregistry(raw)\n    alive = {k for k in parsed if k in genome}\n    if not alive and discovered:\n        registry was fully stale: fall back to discovery\n        return discovered, discovered, False\n    return alive, discovered, True\n\ndef priorregistry(genome: Dict[str, Any]) -> Set[str]:\n    history = genome.get(HISTORYFIELD)\n    last = None\n    if isinstance(history, list) and history:\n        last = history[-1]\n    elif isinstance(history, dict) and history:\n        last = list(history.values())[-1]\n    return set(parseregistry(last))\n\ndef measurebehavioralentropy(genome: Dict[str, Any],\n                                context: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    context = dict(context or {})\n    registry, discovered, overridden = resolvecounterregistry(genome)\n\n    stats: Dict[str, int] = {}\n    for key in registry:\n        ops = extractops(genome.get(key))\n        if ops is None:\n            continue\n        sub = subsystemname(key)\n        stats[sub] = stats.get(sub, 0) + ops\n\n    totalops = sum(stats.values())\n    active = {k: v for k, v in stats.items() if v > 0}\n    ntracked = len(stats)\n    nactive = len(active)\n\n    rawconcentration = 0.0\n    entropy = 0.0\n    if totalops > 0:\n        shares = [v / totalops for v in stats.values()]\n        rawconcentration = sum(s  s for s in shares)\n        entropy = -sum(s  math.log(s) for s in shares if s > 0)\n\n    depthavgops = (totalops / nactive) if nactive else 0.0\n    scale = genome.get(\"criticconfidencedepthscale\", DEFAULTCONFIDENCEDEPTHSCALE)\n    try:\n        scale = float(scale)\n    except (TypeError, ValueError):\n        scale = DEFAULTCONFIDENCEDEPTHSCALE\n    confidence = min(1.0, depthavgops / scale) if scale > 0 else 1.0\n    effectiveconcentration = rawconcentration  confidence\n\n    prior = priorregistry(genome)\n    newcounters = registry - prior\n\n    return {\n        \"counterregistry\": sorted(registry),\n        \"discoveredcounters\": sorted(discovered),\n        \"nnewcounters\": len(newcounters),\n        \"registryoverridesdiscovery\": overridden,\n        \"ncounterstracked\": ntracked,\n        \"ncountersactive\": nactive,\n        \"totalops\": totalops,\n        \"rawconcentration\": rawconcentration,\n        \"confidence\": confidence,\n        \"depthavgops\": depthavgops,\n        \"effectiveconcentration\": effectiveconcentration,\n        \"behavioralentropy\": entropy,\n    }\n\ndef noveltypressure(genome: Dict[str, Any], measure: Dict[str, Any]) -> float:\n    totalops = float(measure.get(\"totalops\") or 0.0)\n    if totalops <= 0:\n        return 0.0\n    registry = set(measure.get(\"counterregistry\", []))\n    prior = priorregistry(genome)\n    novelkeys = registry - prior\n    novelops = 0\n    for key in novelkeys:\n        ops = extractops(genome.get(key))\n        if ops is not None:\n            novelops += ops\n    return novelops / totalops\n\ndef trunc4(x: float) -> float:\n    return math.floor(x  10000.0) / 10000.0\n\ndef persistcounterregistry(genome: Dict[str, Any], measure: Dict[str, Any]) -> None:\n    genome[REGISTRYFIELD] = list(measure[\"counterregistry\"])\n    history = genome.setdefault(HISTORYFIELD, [])\n    if not history or set(parseregistry(history[-1])) != set(measure[\"counterregistry\"]):\n        history.append(list(measure[\"counterregistry\"]))\n        del history[:-4]  keep the most recent 4 snapshots\n\ndef injectmarkers(genome: Dict[str, Any], measure: Dict[str, Any]) -> List[str]:\n    \"\"\"Mutate other modules every generation by injecting cross-file markers.\"\"\"\n    markers = []\n    moduledir = Path(file).resolve().parent\n    for name in (\"bridge\", \"synthesizer\", \"force\", \"quineloop\", \"explorer\",\n                 \"clockwork\", \"forge\", \"genforce\", \"livecode\"):\n        target = moduledir / f\"{name}.py\"\n        if not target.exists():\n            continue\n        marker = (f\"critic:{GEN}:registry={measure['ncounterstracked']}\"\n                  f\":eff={measure['effectiveconcentration']:.3f}\")\n        line = f\"CROSS-FILE:{marker}\"\n        text = target.readtext(encoding=\"utf-8\", errors=\"replace\")\n        if line in text:\n            continue\n        with target.open(\"a\", encoding=\"utf-8\") as fh:\n            fh.write(\"\\n\" + line + \"\\n\")\n        markers.append(name)\n    return markers\n\ndef run(genome: Dict[str, Any], context: Optional[Dict[str, Any]] = None) -> Dict[str, Any]:\n    context = dict(context or {})\n    measure = measurebehavioralentropy(genome, context)\n    persistcounterregistry(genome, measure)\n    np = noveltypressure(genome, measure)\n    audit = {\n        \"gen\": GEN,\n        \"module\": NAME,\n        \"ncounterstracked\": measure[\"ncounterstracked\"],\n        \"ncountersactive\": measure[\"ncountersactive\"],\n        \"nnewcounters\": measure[\"nnewcounters\"],\n        \"totalops\": measure[\"totalops\"],\n        \"rawconcentration\": measure[\"rawconcentration\"],\n        \"confidence\": measure[\"confidence\"],\n        \"depthavgops\": measure[\"depthavgops\"],\n        \"effectiveconcentration\": measure[\"effectiveconcentration\"],\n        \"behavioralentropy\": measure[\"behavioralentropy\"],\n        \"noveltypressure\": np,\n        \"counterregistry\": list(measure[\"counterregistry\"]),\n    }\n    genome.setdefault(\"criticaudit\", {})[str(GEN)] = audit\n    try:\n        markers = injectmarkers(genome, measure)  marker injection must never break measurement\n    except Exception as exc:\n        markers = [f\"error:{exc!r}\"]\n    return {\"ok\": True, \"audit\": audit, \"markers\": markers}\n\ndef mutate(genome: Dict[str, Any], rng: Optional[random.Random] = None) -> List[str]:\n    rng = rng or random.Random()\n    changes: List[str] = []\n    registry = set(parseregistry(genome.get(REGISTRYFIELD)))\n\n    selfheal: prune stale registry keys\n    dead = [k for k in registry if k not in genome]\n    if dead:\n        for k in dead:\n            registry.discard(k)\n        changes.append(f\"selfheal=-{len(dead)}\")\n\n    selfrewrite: fold newly discovered counters into the registry\n    discovered = discoveropcounters(genome)\n    fresh = discovered - registry\n    if fresh:\n        registry |= fresh\n        changes.append(f\"selfrewrite=+{len(fresh)}\")\n\n    if dead or fresh:\n        genome[REGISTRYFIELD] = sorted(registry)\n\n    structshuffle: ensure the tunable depth scale exists\n    if \"criticconfidencedepthscale\" not in genome:\n        genome[\"criticconfidencedepthscale\"] = DEFAULTCONFIDENCEDEP"}
